Subject: [PATCH 0014] skip initialization of overwritten matrix storage and
 predictor copies

Add upperUninitialised/lowerUninitialised without changing existing lduMatrix
accessors. These allocate scalarField(n), without zero fill or copying the
opposite triangle. As with writable accessors, the caller owns subsequent
writes; the new API explicitly requires complete overwrite before any read.
Invalidate lowerCSR on allocation, since an old symmetric cache may refer to
the triangle being replaced.

Use only in newly constructed Gauss convection and laplacian matrices:
- convection's existing fused loop assigns lower=-w*phi and upper=lower+phi
  for every internal face before any coefficient read. This removes one
  lower memset and the former lower-to-upper copy of unneeded values;
- laplacian's existing fused loop assigns upper=deltaCoeffs*gammaMagSf on
  every internal face before any read, removing the upper memset;
- keep diagonal zeros: those loops subtract into the diagonal, including
  cells with no internal faces. Arithmetic and face traversal are unchanged.

Add an fvMatrix boundaryInit constructor overload; the original constructor
still zeroes everything. Only Gauss convection and uncorrected Gauss
laplacian select uninitialised boundary storage. Their complete patch loops
assign internalCoeffs and boundaryCoeffs on every patch (both coupled and
uncoupled laplacian branches). Patch expressions do not read matrix storage.
Empty patches have zero elements. checkImplicit and psi.updateCoeffs only
inspect/update psi; they do not receive this matrix. Source stays zeroed:
convection corrections, corrected laplacian, bounded convection, steadyState
ddt, Sp/SuSp and fvOptions rely on those zeros in +=/-= or as actual values.
No diagonal initialization is removed from Sp/SuSp or relax either.

Add solveWithSource and use it in simpleFoam's momentum predictor. Restrict
copy elision to vector with solveScalar == scalar, exact fvMesh (no virtual solve
override), no implicit/assembled matrix, segregated smoothSolver/GaussSeidel,
all components valid, and positive nSweeps. These match the existing combined
component path in solveSegregated: it creates independent component diagonals,
sources and boundary coefficients. Initial residuals temporarily replace
diag with each component diagonal, then restore its saved bits. Upper,
lower and boundary coefficients are read only. maxIter=0 changes nothing.
Use the identical source += rhs.mesh().V()*rhs.primitiveField() expression
from operator==, then the same solve(controls). Preserve the original source
with a copy and restore by transfer (never floating-point subtraction).
Thus U and solver statistics get identical operands/operations, and UEqn's
A/H/H1 see exactly the original coefficients AND source after the solve.
The copied matrix's optional flux-correction field is unused by this path.
All other cases call the original solve(*this == rhs), retaining its copy.
The tmp<fvMatrix> operator== overload already transfers ownership; do not
consume tUEqn since pEqn.H still needs it after the predictor.

Per step, each of three convection matrices loses one face zero fill and
one face copy, each of four scalar-gamma laplacian matrices (U,p,k,omega)
loses one face zero fill, and all seven lose two patch-coefficient zero fills.
The predictor loses diag/upper/lower and boundary coefficient copies, retaining
one source copy. Estimated profile target: ~20-30 of 2396 samples (0.8-1.3%),
not all 39 initialization samples: diagonal and source zeros remain necessary.
Seven lduMatrix copy-constructor samples and the convection upper copy (2)
are additional evidence for the removed copies, not a measured speedup.

Validation: GCC 13.3 -fsyntax-only with check-all.sh flags/include pattern on
lduMatrix.C, gaussConvectionSchemes.C, gaussLaplacianSchemes.C, simpleFoam.C
and turbulentTransportModels.C. Full bit-identity run remains with the owner.
